{"id": "EUVD-2026-80897", "enisaUuid": "2e7b930a-fed2-35fd-a394-859170e95718", "description": "Scirius through 3.8.0 contains an arbitrary file write vulnerability in the PCAP filestore upload endpoint that allows default User role users to write attacker-controlled JSON content to filesystem paths. Attackers can supply path traversal sequences in the uploaded document's _id field to escape the intended directory and write files with .json extension to arbitrary locations as root.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T17:31:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T14:22:48", "baseScore": 7.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/geo-chen/oss/blob/main/scirius.md", "https://github.com/StamusNetworks/scirius", "https://github.com/StamusNetworks/scirius/blob/3bb49d383f4801b79e6356f9de9f25806afe0311/suricata/rest_api.py#L105-L113", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/scirius-through-3.8.0-arbitrary-file-write-via-pcap-upload"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-92604", "GHSA-h754-2546-79g9"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.58, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4b635b8c-b7d0-3e6e-8cb5-2871988a5658", "product": {"name": "scirius", "vendor": {"name": "StamusNetworks"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.8.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1c5a4437-69b7-3523-8a57-f1a9d05755a2", "vendor": {"name": "StamusNetworks"}}], "isExploited": false}